<!-- ============================== PROCESS ============================== -->
<section class="section" id="process">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <div class="kicker">How it works</div>
      <h2>From raw venue feeds to a single signal.</h2>
      <p>Point Swiftedge at your venues and the composite starts streaming the same second.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="process">
      <div class="step reveal" style="--d:.04s">
        <div class="dot">01</div>
        <h4>Connect</h4>
        <p>Public WebSocket adapters for Binance, Coinbase, and more. No keys, no setup — just live streams.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step reveal" style="--d:.12s">
        <div class="dot">02</div>
        <h4>Classify</h4>
        <p>Aggressor classification at ingest using each venue's native flag — Binance's maker flag, Coinbase's match side.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step reveal" style="--d:.2s">
        <div class="dot">03</div>
        <h4>Aggregate</h4>
        <p>Per-venue and weighted-composite delta, computed per second and per session. Weights are configurable.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step reveal" style="--d:.28s">
        <div class="dot">04</div>
        <h4>Act</h4>
        <p>Divergence reads, alerts, and execution hooks push signal straight into the tools your desk already uses.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================== TRANSPARENCY ============================== -->
<section class="section" id="transparency" style="padding-top:0">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <div class="kicker">Data transparency</div>
      <h2>What's live, what's delayed, and why.</h2>
      <p>
        Every number on this page traces back to a specific public feed.
        No inferred data, no invented prints. Here's exactly where each
        number comes from.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="transparency-grid reveal">
      <article class="trans-card">
        <div class="trans-head">
          <span class="trans-dot" style="background:#4fe3c1"></span>
          <h3>Binance Perp</h3>
          <span class="vc-badge live">live</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          Public WebSocket <code>fstream.binance.com</code>. Every
          <code>aggTrade</code> classified using Binance's <code>m</code> flag
          (maker side). Depth via <code>depth20@100ms</code>. No API key,
          no auth, no rate limit on public streams.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="trans-card">
        <div class="trans-head">
          <span class="trans-dot" style="background:#6f8cff"></span>
          <h3>Coinbase Spot</h3>
          <span class="vc-badge live">live</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          Public WebSocket <code>ws-feed.exchange.coinbase.com</code>.
          <code>matches</code> channel with aggressor inferred by inverting
          the maker-side <code>side</code>. Depth via <code>level2_batch</code>.
          No API key, no auth.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="trans-card">
        <div class="trans-head">
          <span class="trans-dot" style="background:#b06cff"></span>
          <h3>CME Futures</h3>
          <span class="vc-badge delayed">delayed</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          Real-time CME data requires a licensed feed. Currently rendered via
          TradingView's free-tier embed (delayed). <b>Excluded from the
          composite</b> until a licensed feed is connected — no inferred
          contribution, no fake numbers.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="trans-disclosure reveal">
      <b>Session data stays in your browser.</b> Deltas, bars, and venue
      weights are persisted to <code>localStorage</code> on this device only.
      No data is sent to any server. Use the export button in the composite
      panel to download a JSON snapshot, or the reset button to clear it.
      <a href="#" id="btnClearStorage">Clear all session data →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

